---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 08</p>
  <h1>Cardinal numbers <em>0–100</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Numbers run your day: your <strong>age</strong>, a <strong>price</strong>, a <strong>phone number</strong>, a house number. Learn <span class="ex">0–20</span>, the tens, and how to join them with a hyphen — <span class="ex">twenty-one, forty-five, ninety-nine</span>. The hard part is hearing <span class="ex">thirteen</span> versus <span class="ex">thirty</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">-teen / -ty</span>
    <span class="tag">age · prices · numbers</span>
    <span class="tag">10 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Hear thirteen vs thirty.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Tens, ones, and the hyphen.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, and build numbers.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Age, prices, phone numbers.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Two spellings to watch all lesson: <span class="ex">forty</span> (not <span class="ex">fourty</span>) and <span class="ex">ninety</span>. We write joined numbers with a hyphen: <span class="ex">twenty-one</span>.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="where">Where</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="who">Who</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="her">her</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="his">his</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="where" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are you from? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(previous lesson · question words)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya has a new phone. It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="her" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(older lesson · possessives)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>These <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> my keys. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(common contrast · one vs. many)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two numbers that sound close</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">thir<strong>TEEN</strong> (13) &nbsp; · &nbsp; <strong>THIR</strong>ty (30)</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Say both slowly. Where is the <strong>stress</strong> — the loud part — in <span class="ex">thirteen</span>? Where is it in <span class="ex">thirty</span>?</li>
      <li>One word ends in <span class="ex">-teen</span> and one ends in <span class="ex">-ty</span>. Which ending means the smaller number, 13?</li>
      <li>Try the same pair for 14 / 40 and 15 / 50. What stays the same in each pair?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — read the numeral, then choose the word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The number in brackets is your cue — pick the word that matches it exactly</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="thirteen">thirteen</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="thirty">thirty</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fifteen">fifteen</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fifty">fifty</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I am <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="thirty" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> years old. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(30)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The bus is number <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="thirteen" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(13)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The ticket costs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fifty" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dollars. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(50)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>She is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fifteen" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(15)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: ones, tens, and a hyphen</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><strong>0–20 are their own words.</strong> Learn these as whole chunks:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">zero · one · two · three · four · five · six · seven · eight · nine · ten</span><br /><span class="ex">eleven · twelve · thirteen · fourteen · fifteen · sixteen · seventeen · eighteen · nineteen · twenty</span></p>
  <p><strong>The tens climb by ten:</strong></p>
  <p><span class="ex">twenty · thirty · forty · fifty · sixty · seventy · eighty · ninety · one hundred</span></p>
  <p><strong>To make 21–99, join the ten and the one with a hyphen:</strong> &nbsp;<span class="ex">twenty-one (21), thirty-five (35), forty-eight (48), ninety-nine (99)</span>.</p>

  <h3>-teen vs -ty: the table to memorize</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>numeral</th><th>-teen (13–19)</th><th>numeral</th><th>-ty (the tens)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>13</td><td><b>thir</b>teen</td><td>30</td><td><b>thir</b>ty</td></tr>
      <tr><td>14</td><td><b>four</b>teen</td><td>40</td><td><b>for</b>ty <span class="contraction">(no <em>u</em>)</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>15</td><td><b>fif</b>teen</td><td>50</td><td><b>fif</b>ty</td></tr>
      <tr><td>16</td><td><b>six</b>teen</td><td>60</td><td><b>six</b>ty</td></tr>
      <tr><td>17</td><td><b>seven</b>teen</td><td>70</td><td><b>seven</b>ty</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning and spelling check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Stress often helps in clear, careful speech: <span class="ex">thir<strong>TEEN</strong></span> usually has stronger stress at the end, while <span class="ex"><strong>THIR</strong>ty</span> usually has stronger stress at the start. The <span class="ex">-teen</span> words mean 13–19; the <span class="ex">-ty</span> words mean the tens: 20, 30, 40, and so on.</li>
      <li>Is it <span class="ex">fourty</span>? <strong>No.</strong> The number 40 is spelled <span class="ex">forty</span> — drop the <em>u</em> from <em>four</em>.</li>
      <li>Is it <span class="ex">twenty one</span> with a space? In writing we use a hyphen: <span class="ex">twenty-one</span>. The whole number is one tile when we build it.</li>
      <li>What about 100? Say <span class="ex">one hundred</span> (or just <span class="ex">a hundred</span>).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Read the number, say the number</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 1 — match each numeral to its word</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a numeral, then tap the word that fits it. Watch the -teen / -ty endings.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="13">13</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="30">30</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="40">40</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="50">50</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="13" data-placeholder="thirteen">thirteen</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="30" data-placeholder="thirty">thirty</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="40" data-placeholder="forty">forty</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="50" data-placeholder="fifty">fifty</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2 — choose the word for each numeral</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The numeral in brackets is the cue; choose the matching word</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sixteen">sixteen</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sixty">sixty</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="forty">forty</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="ninety">ninety</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="seventy">seventy</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="eighteen">eighteen</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>My address is number <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sixteen" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(16)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>My grandfather is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sixty" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(60)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The jacket costs <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="forty" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dollars. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">($40)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The speed limit is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ninety" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(90)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The meeting room holds <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="seventy" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> people. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(70)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The flight leaves at gate <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="eighteen" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(18)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build it, then say it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i am twenty-five years old">
    <h3>Drill 3 — build your age</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">You are 25. Build the sentence, then say it aloud. The number is one tile.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="years">years</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="twenty-five">twenty-five</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="old">old</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="am">am</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the total is forty dollars">
    <h3>Drill 4 — build the price</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The bill is $40. Build the sentence. Mind the spelling of the number.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="dollars">dollars</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="forty">forty</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="total">total</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="fourty" data-fix="The rent is forty dollars." data-why="The number 40 is spelled forty, with no u — not fourty.">
    <h3>Drill 5 — fix the spelling</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is spelled wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">The</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rent">rent</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="fourty">fourty</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="dollars">dollars.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="thirty" data-fix="My son is thirteen years old." data-why="The cue says 13, so the word is thirteen (-teen), not thirty (30).">
    <h3>Drill 6 — does the word match the number?</h3>
    <p>The cue is <b>(13)</b>. Tap the number word that does not match it.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="my">My</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="son">son is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="thirty">thirty</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="years">years old.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 — say the numeral as a word, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Say the number aloud first. Reveal only after you answer. Watch the hyphen.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> 21 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>twenty-one</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> 40 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>forty</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> 67 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>sixty-seven</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> 90 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>ninety</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> 99 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>ninety-nine</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> 100 &nbsp;→&nbsp; write it in words</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>one hundred</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your age and theirs:</b> Say your real age, then the age of two people in your family. <span class="ex">I am thirty-four. My sister is twenty-nine. My father is sixty-two.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Phone number:</b> Say your phone number slowly, one digit at a time. <span class="ex">five — five — five — one — three — seven…</span> Then say it again a little faster.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Prices at the store:</b> Point at three things and say the price. <span class="ex">This is fifteen dollars. That is forty dollars. The total is fifty-five dollars.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your address:</b> Say your house or apartment number and your floor. <span class="ex">I live at number eighteen. My office is on floor thirteen.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Listen and write:</b> The teacher says a number between 0 and 100; you write the numeral. Then you say a number and the teacher writes it. Watch the -teen / -ty pairs.</div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For 13–19 I use the ending ______. For the tens like 30, 40, 50 I use the ending ______. The loud part of <strong>thirteen</strong> is at the ______; the loud part of <strong>thirty</strong> is at the ______.”</p>
    <p>Then spell two tricky numbers from memory: <strong>40</strong> and <strong>90</strong>. Say one true number sentence about your life right now.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great — you can read, say, and spell numbers 0–100, and tell -teen from -ty.">
    <h3>Final quiz — numbers in real situations</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="thirteen" data-hint="The numeral is 13, so listen for the -teen ending." data-fix="thirteen">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. (13) The bus you need is number ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="thirty">thirty</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="thirteen">thirteen</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="forty">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Which is the correct spelling of 40?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fourty">fourty</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="forty">forty</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fourdy">fourdy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="fifty">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. ($50) The total is ___ dollars.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fifteen">fifteen</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="fifty">fifty</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="five">five</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="twenty-one">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. (21) She is ___ years old.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="twenty one">twenty one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="twentyone">twentyone</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="twenty-one">twenty-one</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="ninety">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. (90) The speed limit is ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="nineteen">nineteen</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ninety">ninety</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="ninty">ninty</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="sixteen">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. (16) My apartment is number ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sixty">sixty</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sixteen">sixteen</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="six">six</button></div>
